## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: 88ddbe5ac6ac5aa0f18ade50aa376b25546fb058

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I used `git log -p` on `ArenaListener.java` to trace the history of the `onFoodLevelChange` method and the `lockFoodLevel` field, searching for prior states of the `if (lockFoodLevel)` check that the fix commit modified.

**(2) The introducing change:** Commit `88ddbe5` ("Lock food level for players in the lobby or spectator area") restructured `onFoodLevelChange`. Previously, the method had an early-return guard:
```java
if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player) || !arena.inArena((Player) event.getEntity()))
    return;
if (lockFoodLevel)
    event.setCancelled(true);
```
This guaranteed the food-lock logic only ever applied to a player actually in the arena. The commit removed this `arena.inArena(p)` check and replaced it with a branch based only on `arena.isRunning()`:
```java
if (arena.isRunning()) {
    if (lockFoodLevel) {
        event.setCancelled(true);
    }
} else {
    if (arena.inLobby(p) || arena.inSpec(p)) {
        event.setCancelled(true);
    }
}
```
The intent was to add lobby/spectator locking for the "not running" case, but in doing so it dropped the per-player `inArena` check for the "running" case — so once the arena was running, `lockFoodLevel` applied to *every* player on the server, not just those in the arena.

**(3) Evidence:** The fix commit `fb5db89` directly restores this guard by changing `if (lockFoodLevel)` to `if (arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel)` in the exact `arena.isRunning()` branch introduced by `88ddbe5`. The diff of `88ddbe5` shows unambiguously that the `arena.inArena(p)` check present before that commit was removed from the running-arena code path, matching the bug description precisely ("affects everyone on the server").

I'm confident in this attribution — the before/after diffs align exactly with the bug description and the fix's target line.

